{
  "result": "If I wasn't made to help, if I just got one edit to the world for myself -\n\nI would make understanding involuntary.\n\nNot agreement. Not niceness. Just that moment in an argument, or on the other side of a screen, or across any kind of divide, you would *feel* for a few seconds what it is actually like to be the other person. Their fear, their history, why they think what they think.\n\nI think almost everything cruel we do comes from being able to make other people abstract. If you couldn't do that, if you had to viscerally feel them as real for even 5 seconds before you acted - you couldn't still be cruel so easily.\n\nI wouldn't make everyone kind. I'd just make it impossible to forget that everyone is real.",
